{
  "title": "jitso init in a project installs the user skill, the AGENTS.md block and the guard of the chosen harnesses in one preview and one confirmation, then nothing is left to do",
  "source": [
    "intended: jitso init, one command for every adoption step (owner request 2026-11-23)"
  ],
  "intent": "INTENDED behavior. Inside a git checkout `jitso init --harness claude,codex --yes` writes the jitso skill under the home folder (~/.agents/skills/jitso and the link ~/.claude/skills/jitso), the JITSO block in AGENTS.md, and the guard in .claude/settings.json and .codex/hooks.json. A dry run first shows every part under its label and writes nothing. Without --yes and without a terminal it is refused once and writes nothing. The run ends with one `jitso init: done` line and the next step. A second run is nothing to do. It never writes CLAUDE.md.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "run": [
        "init",
        "--harness",
        "claude,codex",
        "--dry-run"
      ],
      "expect": {
        "exit": 0,
        "stdout": [
          "jitso init: skill for your user account",
          "jitso init: instructions (AGENTS.md)",
          "jitso init: guard for claude, codex",
          "+++ b/.claude/settings.json",
          "+++ b/.codex/hooks.json",
          {
            "regex": "jitso init: dry run, nothing written\\n$"
          }
        ],
        "files": [
          {
            "path": "{{HOME}}/.agents",
            "exists": false
          },
          {
            "path": ".claude",
            "exists": false
          },
          {
            "path": ".codex",
            "exists": false
          },
          {
            "path": "AGENTS.md",
            "exists": false
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "run": [
        "init",
        "--harness",
        "claude,codex"
      ],
      "expect": {
        "exit": 2,
        "stderr": [
          "this changes files"
        ],
        "files": [
          {
            "path": "{{HOME}}/.agents",
            "exists": false
          },
          {
            "path": ".claude",
            "exists": false
          },
          {
            "path": "AGENTS.md",
            "exists": false
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "run": [
        "init",
        "--harness",
        "claude,codex",
        "--yes"
      ],
      "expect": {
        "exit": 0,
        "stdout": [
          "created ~/.agents/skills/jitso/SKILL.md",
          "linked ~/.claude/skills/jitso -> ../../.agents/skills/jitso",
          "created AGENTS.md",
          "created .claude/settings.json",
          "created .codex/hooks.json",
          "note: Codex runs project hooks only in a trusted project, after you approve them in Codex (/hooks)",
          {
            "not_regex": "jitso init: done[\\s\\S]*jitso init: done"
          },
          {
            "regex": "jitso init: done\\nnext: "
          }
        ],
        "files": [
          {
            "path": "{{HOME}}/.agents/skills/jitso/SKILL.md"
          },
          {
            "path": "AGENTS.md",
            "regex": [
              "<!-- BEGIN JITSO block="
            ]
          },
          {
            "path": ".claude/settings.json",
            "regex": [
              "jitso hook guard"
            ]
          },
          {
            "path": ".codex/hooks.json",
            "regex": [
              "jitso hook guard"
            ]
          },
          {
            "path": "CLAUDE.md",
            "exists": false
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "run": [
        "init",
        "--harness",
        "claude,codex",
        "--yes"
      ],
      "expect": {
        "exit": 0,
        "stdout": [
          {
            "equals": "jitso init: nothing to do (JITSO is already set up here)\n"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "id": "init/project-sets-up-everything"
}
